Corrected non-standard `void main()` to comply with C++ standard.

## Changes

- Changed return type from `void` to `int`
- Added `return 0;` statement
- Added `argc` and `argv` parameters for command-line argument support

```cpp
// Before
void main()
{
    cout<<"Hello world !"<<endl;
    cout<<"Hello world !"<<endl;
}

// After
int main(int argc, char* argv[])
{
    cout<<"Hello world !"<<endl;
    cout<<"Hello world !"<<endl;
    return 0;
}
```

